From 63dc4e06390a023c27ec7b8b3764f9b09cdcdc8d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 16 Oct 2026 16:00:43 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] PETSc: fields of the field split preconditioner by component

Option Fields of PETScLinearSolver and PETScPreconditioner: None (by
default) or Components. With Components, the field split preconditioner
of PETSc (pc_type fieldsplit) receives one field per component of the
unknowns, named after the index of the component: the rows of the true
degrees of freedom of each component, whatever the ordering of the
unknowns (byNODES or byVDIM), which the block size of PETSc does not allow
with the unknowns ordered by nodes. The fields are given after the options
of PETSc and before the setup of the preconditioner, only to an operator
of the size of the finite element space; a preconditioner of PETSc which
preconditions PETScLinearSolver gives its own fields.

Test: an additive field split by component with GAMG on each component
solves the linear elasticity for both orderings, with three fields and
close numbers of iterations, with the Krylov solvers of PETSc and of MFEM;
an invalid value of Fields is refused (1 and 2 processes).
